Dependency Injection (DI)
What is Dependency Injection?
• DI is providing dependencies from outside instead of creating them inside the class.
Types of DI
Constructor Injection
• Dependencies injected through constructor.
• Best for mandatory dependencies.
• Supports immutability and unit testing.
Setter Injection
• Dependencies injected using setter methods.
• Best for optional dependencies.
Field Injection
• Dependencies injected directly into fields using annotations.
Constructor vs Setter Injection
• Constructor: Mandatory dependency.
• Setter: Optional dependency.
When to Use?
• All properties mandatory → Constructor Injection
• Some properties optional → Setter Injection
